Chapter: BvtTableWalks
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeGameRules
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtCheck

 The tavern table walks name their set list once a call (a list constant is built again at every mention, about 1 KB).
 Answers a bit per check: 1 the last backgammon set's index is its place in tbd-sets, 2 a world with no game board
 answers -1 for chess and backgammon boards, 4 those three walks over every set allocate under 8 KB together; -9 is a fixture that did not build. 7 is all.
  btw-run : Integer -> Integer
  btw-run (unused) = when cg-game cg-founding-capacity
    is Err (_) -> -9
    is Ok (game) -> let last = list-at tbd-sets (list-length tbd-sets - 1)
      in let count = list-length tbd-sets
      in let t0 = __heap-save
      in let index = tbd-index last 0
      in let chess = tch-board-set game.world 7 0
      in let backgammon = tbd-board-set game.world 7 0
      in let t1 = __heap-save
      in (if index == count - 1 then 1 else 0) + (if chess == -1 & backgammon == -1 then 2 else 0) + (if t1 - t0 < 8192 then 4 else 0)
  bvt-table-walks : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  bvt-table-walks (unused) = act
    n <- btw-run 0
    a <- bvt-check ("the tavern table walks find a set, answer -1 with no board and name their list once a call (code " & show n & ")") (n == 7)
    a
  end
